{
    // Standard SigmaFi V2 zero-coupon bond.
    // Use only with ZC_Standard_Order and ZC_Standard_BondVault. One script serves ERG and token repayment: the
    // repayment asset is a constant, so each repayment asset has its own bond address and all of
    // them share one template. An indexed node lists one market by ErgoTree and every bond by
    // template hash; a consuming contract pins the tree hash of the asset it expects.
    // The bond is always a single claim (an NFT-style asset). Fractional shares are a separate
    // layer: ZC_Standard_FractionalMint / ZC_Standard_FractionalVault hold the circulating unit.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_VAULT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of ZC_Standard_BondVault; every settlement pays it
    // CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN: Coll[Byte] - repayment token id; EMPTY for ERG repayment
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (bond asset, 2) - the reserve. It is NEVER burned here: it moves to the vault on
    //   settlement, so the box holding 2 units stays the asset's state box (see ZC_Standard_Order).
    // tokens(1..): collateral tokens. The order's tokens, and for a token bond possibly the
    //   repayment token, appended last by a recollateralization.
    //
    // REGISTERS (all pinned by ZC_Standard_Order)
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - originating order id, which is also the bond asset id
    // R5: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the borrower script
    // R6: Coll[Long] - exact copy of the order's borrower values (7..64 Longs):
    //   0 repayment amount; 1 principal nanoERG; 2 repayment ERG floor excluding fee refund;
    //   3 requested maturity height or on-close duration; 4 order expiry height (historical);
    //   5 expiry fee (already refunded); 6 maturity mode; 7.. liquidation payload
    // R7: Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)] - agreed principal tokens
    // ZC_Standard_Order lends only in this bond's repayment asset, so for a bond it created the
    // principal P is R6(1) for ERG (R7 empty) and R7(0)._2 for a token (R7 exactly that token),
    // in the same unit as the repayment R6(0). R6(2) never binds for ERG and is at most 1000000
    // for a token, so R6(0) is the whole repayment. This script does not re-check any of it.
    // R8: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the serialized liquidation expression
    // R9: Coll[Long] - (lender liquidation fee reserve, start height, maturity height)
    // Value minus R9(0) is collateral nanoERG.
    // Creation height: when the bond last moved. The order sets it to the start height R9(1); each
    // recollateralization stamps a new one (see RECOLLATERALIZE).
    //
    // PATHS AND CONTEXT VARS
    // Liquidation: 0 Coll[Byte] liquidation expression; 1 Int settlement output index.
    // Repayment:   1 Int settlement output index; 2 Int collateral-return output index. Vars 0, 3 absent.
    // Recollateralize:      3 Int successor output index. Var 0 absent.
    //
    // SETTLEMENT BOX (both paths), at ZC_Standard_BondVault
    // tokens(0) = this bond's reserve (asset, 2); R4 = SELF.id; R5: Byte = 0 repaid / 1 liquidated.
    // Repayment: tokens are exactly the reserve, plus (repayment token, >= R6(0)) for a token bond;
    //   value >= fee reserve + ERG floor, and >= fee reserve + R6(0) for an ERG bond.
    //   Collateral returns to the borrower script, tagged R4 = SELF.id. Requires HEIGHT < maturity.
    // Liquidation: the agreed expression decides eligibility and the vault's value and tokens(1..).
    //
    // REPAYING FROM COLLATERAL
    // With a borrower-script co-spend, the return box may hold up to R6(0) less of the repayment
    // asset than the bond does: nanoERG for an ERG bond, the repayment token for a token bond. The
    // settlement is unchanged, so the lender is paid exactly the same; the borrower brings only what
    // the collateral does not cover (for a token bond, also the ERG floor beside the token). Every
    // other collateral token returns exactly, and without the co-spend nothing may be kept back, so
    // a third party who repays cannot take any collateral. Without this, a borrower whose spare funds
    // sit in the bond must find the repayment elsewhere or lose everything at maturity liquidation.
    //
    // RECOLLATERALIZE
    // The borrower adds collateral before maturity, e.g. to stay above an oracle ratio. It needs a
    // borrower-script co-spend: an open path would let anyone re-spend the bond and invalidate
    // pending repayments. The successor has this script, identical registers, the same tokens with no
    // amount lower, and more of something: ERG, a held token, or, for a token bond holding none of
    // it, the repayment token appended last. No other new token: every rule values the repayment
    // asset, and a token nobody prices would add nothing.
    // At most once per 60 blocks, counted from the box's creation height. The successor must stamp a
    // creation height within 15 blocks of inclusion, so two recollateralizations land at least 45
    // blocks apart, and a bond maturing within 60 blocks of its start can never be recollateralized.
    // The wait is what stops a borrower dodging a pending liquidation: re-spending the bond voids the
    // liquidator's transaction, but the liquidator rebuilds against the new box, which the borrower
    // cannot move again in time. The box id changes; the asset does not.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // A hand-made box with this script proves nothing: authenticate the asset's order (ZC_Standard_Order).
    // The liquidation expression controls the vault's contents; both parties must inspect it.
    // Anyone may repay in full. Liquidation may run before maturity if the expression allows it.
    // An anyone-can-spend borrower script lets anyone recollateralize or repay from collateral.
    // Storage rent, live-node serialization and maximum cost are unverified.

    val borrower = SELF.R6[Coll[Long]].get
    val lender = SELF.R9[Coll[Long]].get

    if (borrower.size < 7 || borrower.size > 64 || lender.size != 3) {
        sigmaProp(false)
    } else {
        val fee = lender(0)
        val maturity = lender(2)
        val borrowerHash = SELF.R5[Coll[Byte]].get
        val collateral = SELF.tokens.slice(1, SELF.tokens.size)
        val liquidationScript = getVar[Coll[Byte]](0)
        val recollateralizeIndex = getVar[Int](3)
        val repaymentToken = CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN
        // An empty collection taken from the box, not written as a literal. Testing the constant
        // alone (its size) is folded at compile time, which gives the ERG and token bonds different
        // templates and breaks listing every bond by template hash.
        val noToken = SELF.id.slice(0, 0)
        val borrowerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
            b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash
        }

        if (fee < 0L || fee > SELF.value - 1000000L) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else if (liquidationScript.isDefined || !recollateralizeIndex.isDefined) {
            // Settlement: liquidation or repayment
            val settlementIndex = getVar[Int](1).get
            if (settlementIndex < 0 || settlementIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val settlement = OUTPUTS(settlementIndex)
                val toVault =
                    blake2b256(settlement.propositionBytes) == CONST_VAULT_HASH &&
                    settlement.tokens.size > 0 &&
                    settlement.tokens(0) == SELF.tokens(0) &&
                    settlement.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id

                if (liquidationScript.isDefined) {
                    val liquidated =
                        blake2b256(liquidationScript.get) == SELF.R8[Coll[Byte]].get &&
                        toVault &&
                        settlement.R5[Byte].get == 1.toByte
                    sigmaProp(liquidated) && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](0)
                } else {
                    val returnIndex = getVar[Int](2).get
                    if (returnIndex < 0 || returnIndex >= OUTPUTS.size || returnIndex == settlementIndex) {
                        sigmaProp(false)
                    } else {
                        val returnBox = OUTPUTS(returnIndex)
                        val repayment = borrower(0)
                        val repaysERG = repaymentToken == noToken
                        // Subtract the fee refund rather than add to the terms, to avoid overflow.
                        val ergPaid = settlement.value >= fee && settlement.value - fee >= borrower(2)
                        val assetPaid = if (repaysERG) {
                            settlement.tokens.size == 1 && settlement.value - fee >= repayment
                        } else {
                            settlement.tokens.size == 2 &&
                            settlement.tokens(1)._1 == repaymentToken &&
                            settlement.tokens(1)._2 >= repayment
                        }
                        // What the borrower may keep back from the return box, in the repayment asset.
                        val fromCollateral = if (borrowerAuth) repayment else 0L
                        val heldRepayment = collateral.fold(0L, { (a: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            if (t._1 == repaymentToken) a + t._2 else a
                        })
                        val returnedRepayment = returnBox.tokens.fold(0L, { (a: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                            if (t._1 == repaymentToken) a + t._2 else a
                        })
                        val otherCollateral = collateral.filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 != repaymentToken }
                        val otherReturned = returnBox.tokens.filter { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 != repaymentToken }
                        // No overflow: SELF.value - fee is at least 1000000, the repayment at most Long.MaxValue.
                        val ergReturned = if (repaysERG) SELF.value - fee - fromCollateral else SELF.value - fee
                        val collateralReturned =
                            otherReturned == otherCollateral &&
                            returnedRepayment >= heldRepayment - fromCollateral &&
                            returnBox.value >= ergReturned
                        val repaid =
                            HEIGHT.toLong < maturity &&
                            toVault &&
                            settlement.R5[Byte].get == 0.toByte &&
                            ergPaid && assetPaid &&
                            blake2b256(returnBox.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash &&
                            returnBox.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                            collateralReturned
                        sigmaProp(repaid)
                    }
                }
            }
        } else {
            // Recollateralize
            val index = recollateralizeIndex.get
            if (index < 0 || index >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val next = OUTPUTS(index)
                val size = SELF.tokens.size
                val holdsRepayment = collateral.exists { (t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => t._1 == repaymentToken }
                // A token bond holding none of its repayment token may take it on, appended last. No
                // token id equals an ERG bond's empty constant, so an ERG bond can never append.
                // holdsRepayment is defensive: offline signing already refuses a duplicate token id.
                val appended =
                    next.tokens.size == size + 1 &&
                    !holdsRepayment &&
                    next.tokens(size)._1 == repaymentToken
                if (next.tokens.size != size && !appended) {
                    sigmaProp(false)
                } else {
                    val sameTerms =
                        next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                        next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get &&
                        next.R5[Coll[Byte]].get == borrowerHash &&
                        next.R6[Coll[Long]].get == borrower &&
                        next.R7[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get == SELF.R7[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get &&
                        next.R8[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.R8[Coll[Byte]].get &&
                        next.R9[Coll[Long]].get == lender
                    val noneLower =
                        next.value >= SELF.value &&
                        next.tokens(0) == SELF.tokens(0) &&
                        SELF.tokens.indices.forall { (j: Int) =>
                            next.tokens(j)._1 == SELF.tokens(j)._1 && next.tokens(j)._2 >= SELF.tokens(j)._2
                        }
                    val tokenGrown = SELF.tokens.indices.exists { (j: Int) => next.tokens(j)._2 > SELF.tokens(j)._2 }
                    val grown = appended || next.value > SELF.value || tokenGrown
                    // The wait: 60 blocks since the bond last moved, and a fresh stamp on the successor.
                    val stamped = next.creationInfo._1.toLong
                    val rested = HEIGHT.toLong >= SELF.creationInfo._1.toLong + 60L
                    val restamped = stamped >= HEIGHT.toLong - 15L && stamped <= HEIGHT.toLong
                    sigmaProp(
                        HEIGHT.toLong < maturity && borrowerAuth && rested && restamped &&
                        sameTerms && noneLower && grown
                    )
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
